WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.952
TV Quotes lives in the Proposal Engine sidebar,
under Build and estimate.

00:00:04.952 --> 00:00:09.553
It is for the jobs that are TVs rather than LED
walls:

00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:12.621
a model, a quantity and a unit price.

00:00:12.621 --> 00:00:16.456
This walkthrough uses a training example, not a
client record.

00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:19.524
Open TV Quotes and start a new quote.

00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:23.798
Name the quote and the client, then add a TV.

00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:26.337
Pick the model off the LG price list

00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:28.875
and the description and unit cost fill in.

00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:31.414
Set the quantity and where the screens go.

00:00:31.414 --> 00:00:34.905
Add the mounts, the labor and the shipping the same
way.

00:00:34.905 --> 00:00:38.714
The margin applies to every line unless you type
your own price,

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:41.888
and the totals on the right follow as you go.

00:00:42.988 --> 00:00:45.297
When the numbers are right, send it.

00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:47.935
Excel workbook gives you the client quote sheet

00:00:47.935 --> 00:00:51.234
and the internal cost and margin sheet, with live
formulas.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:55.192
Create the client document opens a proposal in the
engine with the

00:00:55.192 --> 00:00:59.810
equipment table, the scope and the totals, ready to
export as PDF or Word.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.104
Then the purchase order.

00:01:02.104 --> 00:01:05.087
Fill in the vendor, who requested it, where it ships

00:01:05.087 --> 00:01:07.474
and when it is needed, and issue it.

00:01:07.474 --> 00:01:09.861
The number is assigned once and never changes,

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:12.248
and the equipment lines go on at cost.

00:01:13.348 --> 00:01:17.952
The PDF is the ANC purchase authorization form,
ready to sign: the

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:22.173
order number, the vendor, the delivery details,
every unit at cost

00:01:22.173 --> 00:01:24.476
and the total for the order.

00:01:25.576 --> 00:01:29.439
And this is the client document, in the standard ANC
format, with

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:32.658
the equipment table, the tax line and the grand
total.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:35.877
Link the CRM deal at the top of the quote,

00:01:35.877 --> 00:01:39.740
and the PO value and the vendor land on that deal
the

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.281
moment the PO is issued, with a note on its
timeline.

00:01:43.281 --> 00:01:46.500
Quote, client document and PO, from one set of
lines.
